        "tag": "title",
        "text": "91"
      },
      {
        "y": 23.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 370.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "One word, many meanings"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 152.7,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Polysemy"
      },
      {
        "y": 88.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 466.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A great many words in English have more than one meaning. Linguists call this aspect of"
      },
      {
        "y": 100.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 190.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "vocabulary polysemy."
      },
      {
        "y": 112.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 494.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Look at these sentences and think about how you would translate the words in italics into your"
      },
      {
        "y": 124.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 160.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "own language."
      },
      {
        "y": 136,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 345.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "fair It’s only fair that we should share the housework."
      },
      {
        "y": 148.4,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 430.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The Frankfurt Book Fair is a very important event for most publishers."
      },
      {
        "y": 160.4,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 389.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The forecast is for the weather to stay fair for the next week."
      },
      {
        "y": 172.4,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 318.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I’ve got fair skin and burn easily in the sun."
      },
      {
        "y": 184.4,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 378.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "His marks in his final exams ranged from excellent to fair."
      },
      {
        "y": 200.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 466.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "flat The firefighters managed to save the children from the burning third-floor flat."
      },
      {
        "y": 212.7,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 364,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The countryside round here is terribly flat and boring."
      },
      {
        "y": 224.7,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 348.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "To join the Fitness Club, you pay a flat fee of £500."
      },
      {
        "y": 236.7,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 258.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The sonata is in B flat minor."
      },
      {
        "y": 248.7,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 325.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "She finished the exercise in five minutes flat."
      },
      {
        "y": 264.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 272.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "capital Fill in the form in capital letters."
      },
      {
        "y": 276.9,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 310.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Wellington is the capital of New Zealand."
      },
      {
        "y": 288.9,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 337.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You need plenty of capital to open a restaurant."
      },
      {
        "y": 300.9,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 385.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Capital punishment has been abolished in many countries."
      },
      {
        "y": 316.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 261.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "mean What does ‘coagulate’ mean?"
      },
      {
        "y": 329.2,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 246.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I didn’t mean to hurt you."
      },
      {
        "y": 341.2,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 293.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "He’s far too mean to buy her flowers."
      },
      {
        "y": 353.2,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 302,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The mean temperature for July is 25oC."
      },
      {
        "y": 365.2,
        "x0": 140.2,
        "x1": 327.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You shouldn’t be so mean to your little sister."
      },
      {
        "y": 381.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 482,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "You probably need a different word to translate fair, flat, capital and mean in each sentence."
      },
      {
        "y": 393.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 508.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Sometimes the meanings are clearly related – flat as in countryside has a connection with flat as in"
      },
      {
        "y": 405.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "apartment in that they both include an idea of being on one level. Sometimes, however, there is no"
      },
      {
        "y": 417.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 507.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "connection at all. For example, the meaning of fair as in Book Fair has no obvious connection with"
      },
      {
        "y": 429,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 508.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "any of the other meanings of fair. Words like this can be called homographs (words with the same"
      },
      {
        "y": 441.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 239.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "spellings but different meanings)."
      },
      {
        "y": 462.4,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 237.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Being aware of polysemy"
      },
      {
        "y": 480.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 371.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "It is useful to be aware of polysemy in English for several reasons."
      },
      {
        "y": 492.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 515.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• You need to remember that the meaning you first learnt for a word may not be the one that it has"
      },
      {
        "y": 504.3,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 181.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "in a new context."
      },
      {
        "y": 516.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 510.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• You need to be aware that in English, words can sometimes be used as different parts of speech."
      },
      {
        "y": 528.3,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 496.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Flat with its apartment meaning, for instance, can become an adjective, e.g. a set of flat keys."
      },
      {
        "y": 540.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 480.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• Learning about the range of meanings that a word can have can help you to learn several"
      },
      {
        "y": 552.3,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 235.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "meanings for the price of one."
      },
      {
        "y": 564.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 521.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• It will also help you to understand jokes in English, as these are often based on polysemous words."
      },
      {
        "y": 587.9,
        "x0": 110.7,
        "x1": 205,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Language help"
      },
      {
        "y": 612.1,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 504.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The context of a word with multiple meanings will usually make it absolutely clear which of the word’s"
      },
      {
        "y": 624.1,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 485.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "possible meanings is intended. So you can understand what, for example, the noun drill probably"
      },
      {
        "y": 636.1,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 480.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "means in (a) a dental context, (b) an army context, (c) a road-building context, or (d) a language-"
      },
      {
        "y": 648.1,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 176.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "learning context."
      }
